=== 6. FINDINGS (technical, verified unless marked) ===
llvm-cbe
- master needs LLVM 22 (it moved to LLVM 20 in Nov 2025); pinned rev 5341f88 works with LLVM 17.
  Its CMakeLists declares cmake_minimum_required 3.4.3 -> CMake>=4 errors; setup.sh passes
  -DCMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM=3.5 -Wno-dev and wipes the build dir before configuring.
- Bugs fixed in the patch: (a) llvm.fshl/fshr unsupported (libc++ string hash uses rotates);
  (b) crash on Itanium ctor/dtor aliases (C1->C2): alignment query on a function type;
  (c) forward prototypes of internal functions lacked `static`;
  (d) NEW option -cbe-explicit-padding: emits each struct padding gap as explicit uint8_t array
      and wraps EVERY record, including the l_array_N_T array-wrapper structs, in
      #pragma pack on / pack off.
- Output facts: GNU-isms everywhere (__attribute__, __forceinline, __builtin_*, C99 stdint types,
  alignment macros); mangled identifiers up to 398 chars (6 over 255, 75 over 28) -> a symbol
  hashing pass is REQUIRED for Plan 9 linkers; a ~40-line program becomes ~11k lines C because
  libc++ templates instantiate -> link all TUs into one module and run globaldce BEFORE cbe.
- Run llvm-link then `opt -passes=internalize,globaldce --internalize-public-api-list=main`.

kencc / Plan 9 C compiler behaviour (goken9cc 6c; real 9front 6c UNVERIFIED)
- No stdint.h, #if, __attribute__, function-type typedefs, ## token pasting, __builtin_*.
  lower.py handles: strips #if blocks/#includes in the preamble, balanced-paren removal of
  __ATTRIBUTELIST__/__attribute__/__*ALIGN__ macros, strips __forceinline/__noreturn/static inline,
  rewrites `typedef R f(args)` to pointer-to-function typedefs, emits 64-bit literals as 123ull/123ll
  (UINT64_C pasting breaks), defines __UNALIGNED_LOAD__, __builtin_unreachable/trap -> abort().
- 6c rounds every struct/union up to a multiple of the word (8 bytes on amd64) -> LLVM byte offsets
  break. In this kencc `#pragma pack on` is true packing (`pack 1` did NOT work).
- The t3 bug (vector<Item> capacity 10 instead of 8, size 22 instead of 20): the [4 x i8] tail-padding
  wrapper struct was outside pack-on, so 6c made it 8 bytes and Item 36 instead of 32. Fixed in cbe.
- Plan 9 libc differences: printf->print (lower step uses a perl s/printf/print/), no %zu,
  LLVM turns memcmp==0 into bcmp, ceilf missing; handled in rt_p9.c.
- Linking with goken: 6l -L $G/ROOT/arch/amd64/lib -H7 -E _main -o t.exe x.6 rt_p9.6 -lc
- 7 integer helper functions (add/sub/lshr/ashr/and/umax) agree between gcc and 6c over ~1,100 input pairs each.
- RISK: goken 6c was killed (likely OOM, exit 137) on one ~4,000-statement straight-line function
  (a test artifact; splitting fixed it). Watch 6c memory on OpenTTD's large functions.

